l,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/123809","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123809","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123809.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123809.patch","merged_at":"2026-09-25T15:55:38Z"},"body":"## What problem(s) does this PR solve?\r\n\r\nThe attempted downcasting to `T *` causes it to use the implicit variant constructor instead.\r\n| Object * | T *|\r\n| :--- | :---|\r\n|<img width=\"838\" height=\"251\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/476a29e9-7b82-4867-b5dd-72bffc49da27\" />|<img width=\"882\" height=\"267\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/357eb940-d89c-43ab-9069-e1aa1de41c26\" />|\r\n\r\n## Additional information\r\n\r\nI picked `static_cast<T *>` instead of `Object::cast_to<T>`, because as far as I know you must guarantee that the type is correct before using `VariantInternalAccessor<T>` so we can skip the null check that is being used in `Object::cast_to<T>`.\r\n\r\nNo AI used.\r\n","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User